/** Why: the reasons, in Works narration, with Wolf's two handwritten asides playing in order. */
---

<section id="why" class="frame sec lift" aria-labelledby="why-h">
  <div class="why why-seq" data-reveal="why">
    <div>
      <h2 id="why-h" class="why-h"><span>I care what we make.</span><span class="and">And why.</span></h2>
      <div class="s1" style="margin-top:22px"><div class="scribble" style="font-size:20px;transform:rotate(-2.5deg);width:max-content">even if I ramble a lot</div></div>
    </div>
    <div style="padding-top:clamp(0px,1vw,10px)">
      <p class="why-p first">I want to make things people can use, get attached to, or get curious about. A daily annoyance is a reason to care. So is the possibility of an experience that doesn’t exist yet.</p>
      <p class="why-p"><span class="emph m1">There’s a lot of thinking behind that.<svg viewBox="0 0 200 9" preserveAspectRatio="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M2 5 C 40 2, 70 8, 110 4 S 170 2, 198 5"></path></svg></span> We ramble, dream, work through details and make plans. We keep exploring what the thing could be while we build it, put it into people’s hands, fix what isn’t working, and rethink what comes next.</p>
      <div style="position:relative">
        <p class="why-p"><span class="emph m2">I have opinions about how things should work.<svg viewBox="0 0 200 9" preserveAspectRatio="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M2 4 C 50 7, 80 1, 120 5 S 175 7, 198 3"></path></svg></span> We keep the reasons behind those choices with the work, so a new version doesn’t quietly forget what mattered. Some decisions hold up. Others change. I want us to understand why.</p>
        <div class="s4" style="margin:-4px 0 0 clamp(0px,18vw,260px)"><div class="scribble" style="font-size:18px;transform:rotate(-3deg);width:max-content">dark first. fight me.</div></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
